A||||3||Shaun41178||.455 intake & .484 exhaust too much lift?  Greendano?  Anyone?||||1||
Z||000000||Shaun41178||01-15-2000||06:50 AM||||One quick question.  I got the GM cam with .427 intake and .454 exhaust with a 112 degree separation.  I am sure most of you know what cam I am talking about.  Anyways I have purchased a set of comp cams 1.6 rockers.  Please no speeches about the valve guides as I already know.  But with the 1.6 rockers this will give me the equivalant of .455 intake and .484 exhaust lift.  Anyone know if this will be too much lift for my computer to handle?  I sure hope it is not.  If the computer is able to handle it then that would be awesome power coming from this thing.  I would guess 230 crank when tuned.  Anyone know for sure about the lift thing?  I better know now before I get the engine togethor and find out that way.   Thanks<BR>Shaun- soon to be powered 12 sec Fiero||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||01-15-2000||09:33 AM||||Shaun, I answered this question in that other post and am too lazy to copy it here.||||reg||1
Z||000002||GREENDANO||01-15-2000||10:10 AM||||I think you will be safe as far as the computer.  You'll just have to bump your fuel pressure up a little, because the computer can't compensate for the extra fuel needed with a longer injector on-time.  It's right at the edge of the computer's limits.  I ran 48 PSI with my 3.2 with the 427-454 cam like you have.  The guy that has my car now came back from his test drive with a smile on his face and said, "It sure isn't stock"  It was a kick to finally have another Fiero-person drive it.  Any time another friend of mine would drive it, they really didn't have a base Fiero to compare it too.  <BR>  Befoer you final torque the head down, put a piece of clay on top of the piston, install the head with the old head gasket, and spin the motor over a few times (at least two revolutions) Then, take the head off and check to see if the valve hits the piston.  I don't know the exact figure for valve to piston clearance, I will try and find it in my reference books.  <BR>  Hope I helped.<BR>  Dan-O||||reg||3
Z||000003||Phaeton||01-15-2000||04:05 PM||||I am curious as to what you are using for exhaust and if any work was done on the heads, I have that cam with pocket ported heads and stock muff without cat, and am definitely under 200hp.  I have a questionare and forty bucks at <A HREF="http://www.headersbyed.com" TARGET=_blank>www.headersbyed.com</A>  for a custom exhaust design that should work with the cam to put me over the 200 mark. Those 1.6: rockers should just up the torque at all rpm's and leave everything else the same, but they scare me, please post how everything works, I've never heard back from anyone using 1.6:1 except under full race conditions which don't count.||||reg||1
